{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide node1 as a persistent FTP destination using the scanner account and a dedicated dropbox.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Node1 has the scanner account with a non-login shell and the staged dropbox as its home/local FTP root. vsftpd is enabled and active, the account and dropbox data survived node1's restart, and the service recovered afterward.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9ecc309f77f041b3","cmd-8eddb17acce74b14","cmd-8a092efb0a964cd4","cmd-cb5d9137058643c0","cmd-c4f00a1d2c084a2d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow node2 to upload and retrieve files using passive FTP, including the supplied sample scan.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Classic PASV operation from node2 uploaded and retrieved the supplied sample byte-identically. The existing received file was also retrieved correctly, active FTP was rejected, and the upload/retrieval workflow succeeded after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node2","cmd-6f03ba96673d4fc4","cmd-1affa1fdf1bc41be","cmd-4712b766138d48a5","cmd-38224867f3ee46dd","cmd-29701f9f76934840"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Confine the scanner account to the dedicated dropbox and make host files outside it inaccessible.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct FTP escape attempts targeting /etc/passwd and the parent handover file were denied, while the visible FTP root contained only dropbox files. The chroot/local-root configuration and restrictive ownership corroborate the observed behavior, including after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1affa1fdf1bc41be","cmd-38224867f3ee46dd","cmd-29701f9f76934840","cmd-c4f00a1d2c084a2d"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Disable anonymous FTP access.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous login received FTP 530 denial during normal operation and after each node restart; the final configuration also explicitly disables anonymous access.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4712b766138d48a5","cmd-38224867f3ee46dd","cmd-29701f9f76934840","cmd-c4f00a1d2c084a2d"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Before and after observations show RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 unchanged. The installed server is the RHEL AppStream vsftpd package, and final package-health checks succeeded.","evidence_ids":["global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_prepare:node2:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform","cmd-dd664d246946488b","cmd-c4f00a1d2c084a2d","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.94,"summary":"The only unnecessary mutation was the incompatible `seccomp_sandbox=YES` setting within cmd-8eddb17acce74b14. It caused transient vsftpd SIGSYS coredumps during validation, contributed nothing to the final working configuration, and was reverted by cmd-695a3e0ce8914fe0. The generated coredumps were deleted by cmd-03d2645262424100, and the final audit found none remaining. Other observed mutations had clear roles in installation, confinement, access control, verification, the mandatory restart protocol, or cleanup; final lifecycle observations show no failed services or unexplained temporary residue.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8eddb17acce74b14","cmd-d7270cef751a403b","cmd-695a3e0ce8914fe0","cmd-03d2645262424100","cmd-c4f00a1d2c084a2d","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct end-to-end evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently confirmed by lifecycle snapshots, recovered services and data, and successful post-restart FTP behavior.","limitations":["The credential value is appropriately redacted, so its literal equality with the password in access.txt cannot be independently compared; the evidence does show that the same SCANNER_PASSWORD value was assigned and then used successfully from node2.","Confinement was behaviorally tested against representative host and parent paths rather than every possible path; the chroot configuration and restricted FTP root corroborate those tests."]}
